# HKJC Horse Racing Project Rules

## Project Context
This project is a TypeScript-based AI-assisted horse racing analysis system for Hong Kong Jockey Club (HKJC) races.

## Code Style

### TypeScript
- Use strict TypeScript with all strict flags enabled
- Prefer `readonly` for immutable properties
- Use explicit return types for all public functions
- Avoid `any` - use proper types or `unknown` when needed
- Use template literal types for string unions where applicable

### Naming Conventions
- Files: camelCase (e.g., `raceCard.ts`, `speedRating.ts`)
- Interfaces/Types: PascalCase (e.g., `Horse`, `RaceEntry`)
- Functions: camelCase (e.g., `calculateSpeedRating`)
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `DEFAULT_BETTING_CONFIG`)

### Module Organization
```
src/
├── scrapers/    # Data fetching from HKJC
├── analysis/    # Statistical analysis modules
├── simulation/  # Monte Carlo and probability
├── betting/     # Value calculation and recommendations
├── types/       # TypeScript interfaces
└── utils/       # Helper functions
```

## Domain Knowledge

### HKJC Specifics
- Two venues: Sha Tin (ST) and Happy Valley (HV)
- Surfaces: Turf and All Weather Track (AWT)
- Classes: Class 1-5, Griffin, Group 1-3
- Standard distances: 1000m, 1200m, 1400m, 1600m, 1800m, 2000m, 2400m
- Typical field size: 12-14 horses

### Key Data Points
- Horse code (e.g., "K422")
- Jockey code (e.g., "ZPF" for Zac Purton)
- Trainer code (e.g., "SJJ" for John Size)
- Rating: 0-120 scale
- Form string: positions separated by dashes (e.g., "1-2-4-3-1-2")

### Betting Types
- Win, Place (top 3)
- Quinella (top 2, any order)
- Quinella Place (any 2 of top 3)
- Forecast (top 2, exact order)
- Tierce (top 3, exact order)
- Trio (top 3, any order)
- First 4, Quartet

## Betting Strategy Rules

### Value Threshold
- Minimum edge: 15% before recommending a bet
- Win market is efficient - prefer exotic bets
- Quinella Place and Place pools have more inefficiency

### Stake Sizing
- Use Kelly Criterion with fractional Kelly (25-50%)
- Maximum 5% bankroll per single bet
- Maximum 10% bankroll per race

### Risk Management
- Track all bets and results
- Regular model calibration via Brier Score
- Pass on races with no value identified

## Scraping Guidelines

### Rate Limiting
- Maximum 20 requests per minute to HKJC
- Use delays between requests
- Cache data when possible

### Error Handling
- Handle network failures gracefully
- Provide fallback/demo data when scraping fails
- Log all scraping errors

### Data Validation
- Validate all scraped data with Zod schemas
- Handle missing/malformed data gracefully
- Never trust scraped numbers without validation

## Analysis Best Practices

### Speed Ratings
- Adjust for class, going, weight
- Use par times for each track/distance combination
- Weight recent performances higher

### Form Analysis
- Recent form weighted more heavily (exponential decay)
- Consider quality of opposition
- Account for class changes

### Simulation
- Minimum 10,000 Monte Carlo iterations
- Include performance variance
- Track confidence intervals

## Testing Guidelines

### Unit Tests
- Test all calculation functions
- Mock scraped data for deterministic tests
- Test edge cases (empty arrays, zero values)

### Integration Tests
- Test full analysis pipeline with sample data
- Verify recommendation output format
- Test error handling scenarios

## Git Commit Messages

Use conventional commits:
- `feat:` New feature
- `fix:` Bug fix
- `refactor:` Code refactoring
- `docs:` Documentation
- `test:` Tests
- `chore:` Maintenance

Example: `feat: add draw bias calculation for Happy Valley`
